<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15924" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĕpīcrătes</span></b> ,
			ae, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐπικρατής</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The victorious</i>, <i>supreme;</i>
			so Cicero names Pompey, <i><span class="en">Att. 2, 3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A philosopher</i> or <i>rhetorician of
				Athens</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fil. Fam. 16,
			21</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A native of Agyrium</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2,
				2, 9</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
